  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only config so far is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 acc. We know multiprofile substantially helped pca_n2000 (config_002: 0.591 vs config_001: 0.485), but we have no data on whether the multiprofile advantage holds for the learned scvi_n200 representation. Image modality is very weak standalone (~0.22), making RNA-side design decisions the highest-priority question. Question: config_004 (scvi_n200, singleprofile, no aggregation) isolates the profile-setting effect for the best encoder by changing only profile_setting relative to config_005. If config_004 approaches 0.650, the learned latent is robust to profile aggregation and the simpler singleprofile model suffices; if it drops substantially, multiprofile aggregation is confirmed as essential regardless of encoder. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a clean one-variable comparison with the current best, directly tests an important and still-uncertain design axis (profile setting) for the strongest encoder, and avoids prematurely committing budget to multimodal fusion when the image branch is so weak. It reduces uncertainty about whether we can simplify the pipeline before investing in more complex multimodal combinations."
}

